# Context budget (Cursor)

## Gate tools (wave review, wrap-up, duel model gate)

- MCP returns **compact** payload: `gateMeta`, `askQuestion`, `actions` — **not** full `userGate.options` or `coordinatorAction` strings.
- **Do not** paste or summarize the whole tool JSON in chat.
- Call **`AskQuestion`** once with `data.askQuestion`; map the clicked id via `data.actions` (e.g. `looks-good-all`, `fresh-eyes`).
- Phase docs: `start_review` / `start_wrapup` / etc. — one phase per turn.
- `/start` boot: `flywheel_observe` (compact) → `flywheel_start_menu` or `start_ceremony` (~9k) → `start_discover` (~2–3k) only when Step 0 routes past the menu.
- **Never** load ceremony + discover + a phase skill in one turn.

## flywheel_get_skill

- Default: text is a **pointer**; body is in `structuredContent.data.skill.body` only.
- Do **not** call `includeBodyInText: true` unless the user explicitly needs a markdown dump in chat.
- Do **not** load multiple phase skills in one turn (pick one: `start_review`, `start_implement`, `start_wrapup`, `start_planning`).

## Recovery (`/recover-gates`)

- `flywheel_wave_review_gate` → AskQuestion → execute action → optional `flywheel_wrap_up_gate`.
- Skip `br list` if bead ids are already in `gateMeta.beadIds`.
- Skip reading `.pi-flywheel/checkpoint.json` unless phase/beads are unknown.
- On empty `beadIds`, use `suggestedBeadIds` from the gate error payload before asking the user.
- When `wrap_up_already_confirmed`, surface `confirmedAction` / `nextSkill` — do **not** re-open the wrap-up menu unless the user asks.
- **Never** load `start_ceremony`, `start_discover`, or the full `start` / `/start` body for recovery — only `start_review` / `start_wrapup` on demand after a gate action.

## Avoid unless necessary

- `flywheel_capabilities` / `flywheel_robot_docs` (large contract dumps)
- `start_ceremony` / `start_discover` or multiple phase skills in recover/review-only sessions
- Re-reading the same command `.md` file after MCP already returned the gate
